# This spec file is read by gcc when linking.  It is used to specify the
# standard libraries we need in order to link with various sanitizer libs.
# MinGW-lite: generated from this template by module/ABB._asan(); the
# @link_libasan@ placeholder is substituted per profile thread model.
#
# The GCC driver always emits `-lasan` for -fsanitize=address (gcc/gcc.cc
# LIBASAN_SPEC).  This spec's *link_libasan is additionally pulled in only under
# -static-libasan / -static via `%:include(libsanitizer.spec)%(link_libasan)`,
# supplying the transitive dependencies (thread runtime + Win32 import libs)
# that a static libasan.a cannot carry on PE/COFF.

*link_libasan: @link_libasan@

*link_libhwasan: @link_libasan@

*link_libtsan: @link_libasan@

*link_libubsan: @link_libasan@

*link_liblsan: @link_libasan@
